# The worker check's stack in CI's `self-host` job (.github/workflows/ci.yml): the webhook
# worker as a service of its own (docs/self-host.md, "The webhook worker as its own service";
# scripts/worker-check/check.ts). A test fixture, read only as
#
#   docker compose -p self-host-worker --env-file docker/self-host/worker.env ...
#
# Host ports of its own, beside the job's two other stacks, and one setting: deliveries are
# the worker's alone, on every container. Nothing else, `ENVIRONMENT` least of all: the stack
# runs in the tier the others run in, and the receiver is reached within the outbound
# guard's rules (docker/worker-check/compose.yml). The instance admin token is generated by
# the job for each run, never written here.
POSTGRES_PORT=5434
REDIS_PORT=6381
MAILPIT_SMTP_PORT=1027
MAILPIT_UI_PORT=8027
API_PORT=3023
API_2_PORT=3024
LB_PORT=3025
WEBHOOK_WORKER=separate
